From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Subtitles: fewer settings - repair on or off, translate off,
 by hand or automatic

Subtitles had nine settings, four of them under "Repair text subtitles"
and two asking what only the code knows - which languages' letters to
correct, and whether the model reads every line or the doubted words.
Now there are five.

"Repair subtitles" is on or off. On does every repair there is - each
only changes what is plainly broken: the encoding, music notes,
advertising and credit lines, timing that flashes by or overlaps, and
the letters an image conversion misreads, in the subtitle's own
language. The list of languages is gone: the language pack of a
subtitle's language is installed in the background the first time one
in it is read, if the repositories offer one, and the subtitle after it
has it. With an AI provider chosen its model checks the words the
repair doubts; every line was rarely worth its requests.

"AI translate subtitles" is Off, By hand - the subtitle dialog's
Translate to button only - or Automatic, which also starts a video with
no full subtitle in the viewer's language translated into it. The track
it starts from is a full one in the language spoken, else English, else
the first, text before pictures in each: a film's own language is
closest to what is said.

The callback and option filler the language list had are left
registered, unused, so Kodi's settings code is not touched again; they
go when this is folded into the patches that added them.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
